WEBVTT

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:44.740
Give me a break...

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:46.620
We always have to deal with things like this...

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:52.770
Cease your resistance and surrender!

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:56.030
No chance in hell that'll happen.

00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:57.200
Nope.

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:00.310
Don't tell me-

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:01.100
You're kidding me.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:03.110
We never heard about this.

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:05.140
Shall we retreat?

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:06.970
Do not fear.

00:02:06.970 --> 00:02:09.230
We cannot allow one tank to slow us down!

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:15.500
Shit...

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:39.420
LT,

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:41.140
I've confirmed the survival of the corporal.

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:42.000
Copy that.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.240
As reckless as always.

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:46.150
Sorry...

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:48.160
It's in tatters.

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:53.100
I'm referring to your army uniform.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:54.790
Ohh...

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:14.140
Umm, where's everybody?

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:16.880
Captain Hunks is giving his report of this incident.

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:20.150
Oreld and Machs are at the infirmary,

00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:24.650
and I'm sure Oreld's hitting on the female doctors.

00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:29.100
And the lieutenant?

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:30.920
Alice is...

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:35.110
Where is Alice?

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:38.300
Sister, please open the door!

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:40.390
Taking on a tank by yourself...

00:03:40.390 --> 00:03:42.140
Cool your head in there!

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:43.920
But that was my mission!

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:45.870
You're grounded!

00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:48.270
Forgive us, Alice.

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:51.400
Elice just wants you to be safe.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:54.010
I'm telling you to wake up already!

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:56.530
To be taking on tanks in a peaceful time like this...

00:03:56.530 --> 00:03:58.380
Quit that commission already!

00:03:58.380 --> 00:03:59.760
Indeed!

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:04.040
We wouldn't be able to face your fiancé if you were to scar your face.

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:05.550
Exactly!

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:10.390
But gosh, you really have a lot of luck, Corporal.

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:15.740
Your uniform is all ragged, yet you are completely fine.

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:17.740
Sorry...

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:19.460
I'm even having you do things like this for me.

00:04:19.460 --> 00:04:21.790
Oh, no, no, don't worry about it.

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:24.080
This is one of my important duties.

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:26.140
Ow!

00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:27.170
Are you okay?

00:04:27.170 --> 00:04:28.690
Let me get some medicine!

00:04:28.690 --> 00:04:30.310
Oh, this is nothing.

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:31.580
B-But...

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:32.080
Attention!

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:35.510
Soldiers should always remain calm!

00:04:35.510 --> 00:04:35.870
Yes, sir!

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:40.380
...Would be something Alice would say, right?

00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:43.880
Yeah...

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:47.300
Oreld was complaining that...

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:52.130
...ever since you joined, Section III's missions have become very hard ones, Corporal.

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:55.120
So, it's because of me after all-

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:56.040
No, no.

00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:58.140
Oreld's the one saying weird things.

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:03.170
"I didn't think I'd be firing rifles after joining the army"...

00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:05.110
...was one of his complaints, so...

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:10.590
If you don't ever have to fire a rifle, then that's all for the better.

00:05:13.490 --> 00:05:14.330
But, yeah...

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:16.220
...Section III has changed.

00:05:16.570 --> 00:05:18.290
It's completely different than what happened in the beginning.

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:20.250
In the beginning?

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:21.110
Yes.

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:24.160
Only the captain and I were here at first.

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:27.980
Don't be deceived; I'm the longest-serving member here.

00:05:29.450 --> 00:05:32.250
Even the lieutenant wasn't here?

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:35.500
Oreld got assigned here after me...

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:37.380
...and after a while, Machs.

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:40.340
Alice came after that.

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:41.820
That reminds me,

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:45.830
when Machs first came here, he looked so weird.

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:47.530
He said, "Ughh".

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:54.780
A year ago, Machs was at a different post.

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:59.080
I think it was called the elite course or something like that...

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:02.920
Sergeant Major Machs reporting.

00:06:03.370 --> 00:06:04.150
Come in.

00:06:10.360 --> 00:06:13.000
I've come to talk about the war relief supplies-

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:13.550
The decision has already been made for that!
I've come to talk about the war relief supplies-

00:06:13.550 --> 00:06:15.430
The decision has already been made for that!

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:18.260
Major, please rethink this!

00:06:18.260 --> 00:06:21.730
The price of the cans from Shtern is half of those from Jingetsu.

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:23.920
We can send twice the amount of the supplies!

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:25.320
The major is busy!

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:26.510
Major!

00:06:28.140 --> 00:06:29.090
Machs.

00:06:29.810 --> 00:06:32.820
What have you learned at the academy?

00:06:33.970 --> 00:06:37.830
A soldier's duty is to abide his superior's orders;

00:06:38.350 --> 00:06:42.560
it's not to interfere with battle plans with his own judgment.

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:43.590
Major...

00:06:43.850 --> 00:06:44.920
Machs.

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:46.710
The major is a person with a tolerant personality,

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:48.740
and he has a high regard for your abilities.

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:52.630
However, if you are going to interfere further with the mission, then...

00:06:55.970 --> 00:06:57.110
Excuse me.

00:07:08.210 --> 00:07:10.170
Shall I make you a drink?

00:07:10.670 --> 00:07:12.110
Tomato juice...

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:13.890
Nah, give me some beer.

00:07:13.890 --> 00:07:15.040
Understood.

00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:25.750
Yo, it's been a while.

00:07:28.350 --> 00:07:29.550
I'm shocked...

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:30.740
You're an officer?

00:07:30.740 --> 00:07:32.460
How did you dig your way up?

00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:34.770
Skills, man.

00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:38.000
And thus, the prestige of the army has fallen.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:42.020
Yeah, I mean a punk like me can serve as an officer.

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:43.250
Yo, let me be already!

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:45.360
But, why did you decide to enlist?

00:07:45.570 --> 00:07:49.520
Well, I couldn't just screw around for my entire life.

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:52.760
And the place that guarantees
you food these days is the army, right?

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:57.650
The war's over, so there's no chance I'll be sent to the front lines now.

00:08:02.990 --> 00:08:08.800
"We're able to enjoy drinking beer today because of the great army~", eh?

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:10.510
What's the matter with you?

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:11.460
Nothing.

00:08:11.460 --> 00:08:13.140
Got some worries?

00:08:14.480 --> 00:08:15.290
Oh, I know.

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:16.540
You got dumped.

00:08:16.540 --> 00:08:17.490
I see.

00:08:17.490 --> 00:08:19.100
So that's why you're in a place like this.

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:22.520
You've always been kind of clumsy.

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:23.690
So who's the lady?

00:08:23.690 --> 00:08:25.550
A cute little nurse?

00:08:25.550 --> 00:08:27.330
If that's the case, I can-

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:28.230
It's not that!!!

00:08:34.720 --> 00:08:35.610
Hey...

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:38.590
BEER!

00:08:41.190 --> 00:08:43.420
Aww, what a waste.

00:08:43.420 --> 00:08:46.580
You'll receive divine retribution if you waste beer like that.

00:08:47.240 --> 00:08:50.230
So, how about coming over to my section?

00:08:50.230 --> 00:08:53.470
At this rate, you can't really stay at your current post, right?

00:08:53.470 --> 00:08:55.430
The post just got set up,

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:56.840
but it feels nice there.

00:08:57.860 --> 00:09:00.100
It's called Imperial S.S. III.

00:09:00.340 --> 00:09:02.250
Section III?!

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:05.560
That place built as an excuse for the military-

00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:08.520
At least there's no corruption there.

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:11.850
Well, money doesn't really go there much, either.

00:09:11.850 --> 00:09:13.140
Shut up!

00:09:13.140 --> 00:09:15.230
I... I...

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:19.130
You're hopeless, man.

00:09:22.310 --> 00:09:23.940
I'm to be assigned to a reserve.

00:09:25.950 --> 00:09:27.350
This is to get rid of a nuisance like me, huh?

00:09:27.350 --> 00:09:28.910
Watch your mouth, Machs!

00:09:29.730 --> 00:09:31.840
You're not suited for being a soldier.

00:09:32.430 --> 00:09:36.390
Go get exposed to the world and cool your head a bit.

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:41.580
Boss, I caught some game.

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:42.670
Game?!

00:09:49.290 --> 00:09:50.410
Ugh?!!!

00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:54.150
You can't do that, Mer-kun.

00:09:54.730 --> 00:09:57.000
Don't be licking our guest's face.

00:10:03.900 --> 00:10:07.850
Ah, you're not a guest, but our fourth member.

00:10:07.850 --> 00:10:09.250
Fourth member?

00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:11.960
We'll be getting another member soon, though.

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:13.640
Captain Hunks.

00:10:13.640 --> 00:10:15.050
The boss over here.

00:10:15.050 --> 00:10:16.900
And this is Stekkin.

00:10:16.900 --> 00:10:18.120
I'm a master sergeant.

00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:21.310
As you can see, we're short on hands here.

00:10:21.310 --> 00:10:23.140
You're doing a lot for us by coming over.

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:25.390
Just choose a seat you like.

00:10:25.880 --> 00:10:27.490
I'll make some tea for you now.

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:31.530
I'm grateful, but I don't plan on coming here.

00:10:31.530 --> 00:10:32.650
H-Hey!

00:10:33.620 --> 00:10:34.580
Sorry.

00:10:34.580 --> 00:10:37.710
It's way too early to be thinking that you're suffering a setback.

00:10:38.630 --> 00:10:41.450
You can choose to give up anytime.

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:43.730
You've done your investigation, right?

00:10:44.930 --> 00:10:47.370
I'm talking about the corruption issue with Major Ranke.

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:53.460
You're going to pick up the case?

00:10:53.650 --> 00:10:56.200
That depends on your investigation report.

00:10:57.100 --> 00:10:57.930
So, what about it?

00:10:57.930 --> 00:10:58.970
Do you want to give it a try?

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:08.640
Look forward to working with ya, Sergeant Major Machs.

00:11:09.130 --> 00:11:12.780
Yo man... be more considerate of me...

00:11:12.780 --> 00:11:15.400
...when I'm stuck in this post with that one girl.

00:11:19.190 --> 00:11:19.990
Oh, my.

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:20.740
She's gone.

00:11:21.850 --> 00:11:23.300
She got away?!

00:11:26.820 --> 00:11:31.120
With the captain's help,
Machs smoothly entered into Section III.

00:11:33.110 --> 00:11:34.280
Here you go.

00:11:38.360 --> 00:11:39.820
Here you go.

00:11:40.290 --> 00:11:42.280
This is Section III's task?

00:11:42.280 --> 00:11:44.270
"War relief".

00:11:44.270 --> 00:11:45.220
Not happy with that?

00:11:45.580 --> 00:11:46.550
Not really.

00:11:48.080 --> 00:11:50.890
It's impossible for Section III to do anything.

00:11:51.750 --> 00:11:53.810
What are you getting all pissed off about?

00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:57.060
Is this about your superior?

00:11:57.060 --> 00:11:59.840
You do know that it's because the boss hasn't gotten-

00:11:59.840 --> 00:12:00.600
Hey, hurry up, man.
You do know that it's because the boss hasn't gotten-

00:12:00.600 --> 00:12:02.010
Hey, hurry up, man.

00:12:02.140 --> 00:12:02.700
Yes, yes.

00:12:03.210 --> 00:12:04.640
That's what he says,

00:12:04.640 --> 00:12:06.700
but in the end, he's just going to throw it aside, too.

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:07.740
You dumb boy.

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:10.870
The boss is being considerate of you.

00:12:10.870 --> 00:12:12.120
Here you go.

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:20.720
I thought maybe I could do something if I joined the army.

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:23.590
Don't be talking about your dreams in a place like this, yo.

00:12:24.010 --> 00:12:25.720
Sergeant Major Machs!

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:29.720
I heard that you'd transferred to Section III,

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:31.540
but this is what you're doing?

00:12:32.260 --> 00:12:34.950
You, one of the top students in the Academy.

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:40.090
Maybe you should've resigned from the army like the major said.

00:12:40.520 --> 00:12:42.010
It's sad to see you like this.

00:12:42.690 --> 00:12:44.550
Only one bowl per person.

00:12:44.550 --> 00:12:46.110
Take it and leave, please.

00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:48.040
There are still people waiting behind you.

00:12:48.040 --> 00:12:48.880
Why you!

00:12:49.510 --> 00:12:52.000
Once you're done eating, dishes go there.

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:58.490
Well, do your best in raising the army's image.

00:13:01.590 --> 00:13:03.410
What a messed up bastard.

00:13:03.860 --> 00:13:05.630
Okay, we're getting rid of our bad luck;

00:13:05.630 --> 00:13:07.260
we're going drinking tonight.

00:13:08.620 --> 00:13:10.150
My head hurts.

00:13:10.150 --> 00:13:13.060
You're not a drinker, and you drank way too much.

00:13:13.230 --> 00:13:13.930
You are late!

00:13:14.970 --> 00:13:16.830
Soldiers should be punctual!

00:13:16.830 --> 00:13:18.410
Tardiness cannot be tolerated!

00:13:19.450 --> 00:13:21.120
What's this smell?!

00:13:21.120 --> 00:13:22.130
Sorry.

00:13:22.130 --> 00:13:24.280
Ahh, we drank a bit too much.

00:13:24.500 --> 00:13:25.870
You guys are too relaxed!

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:28.160
Wh-Who are you?

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:31.160
2nd Lieutenant Alice L. Malvin.

00:13:31.530 --> 00:13:36.120
The lieutenant has come to serve as Section III's LT.

00:13:38.520 --> 00:13:40.130
There you have it.

00:13:40.330 --> 00:13:44.810
Then, could you tell her to put her sword down?

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:48.090
She's a successor to one of the Thirteen Appointed Families?!

00:13:48.550 --> 00:13:49.860
Apparently.

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:53.090
What's the child of such high nobility doing here?

00:13:53.090 --> 00:13:55.600
Must be a noble princess's whim, right?

00:13:56.740 --> 00:13:57.810
In other words,

00:13:57.810 --> 00:14:00.400
noble children that the army considers troublemakers...

00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:04.110
...are sent to worthless posts as decoration.

00:14:04.330 --> 00:14:06.010
Oh, Machs.

00:14:06.010 --> 00:14:08.610
You've become such a bitter person.

00:14:12.850 --> 00:14:14.580
But yeah, this is a headache.

00:14:15.100 --> 00:14:18.080
We have to deal with a noble's hobby.

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:19.250
Did I hear something about nobles?

00:14:22.630 --> 00:14:24.630
May I sit there?

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:26.190
Go... Go right ahead.

00:14:30.020 --> 00:14:33.570
I thought I could promote bonding as we eat lunch together.

00:14:33.570 --> 00:14:35.010
Oh, that's so nice of you.

00:14:35.260 --> 00:14:36.690
Are your missions coming along well?

00:14:36.690 --> 00:14:38.520
Not too bad.

00:14:39.130 --> 00:14:40.200
What is the matter?

00:14:40.200 --> 00:14:42.510
I can help if there is something you are worried about.

00:14:42.510 --> 00:14:45.780
I am devoting my life to war relief.

00:14:46.460 --> 00:14:48.330
No matter how small the problem is, I-

00:14:48.330 --> 00:14:49.760
Excuse me.

00:14:49.760 --> 00:14:51.530
You still have some stew.

00:14:54.340 --> 00:14:56.880
Ah, he doesn't eat too much.

00:14:58.410 --> 00:14:59.650
That's not good.

00:14:59.650 --> 00:15:01.970
Stamina is the most important thing for soldiers.

00:15:01.970 --> 00:15:03.980
We must eat when we can.

00:15:04.890 --> 00:15:06.600
I'll talk to you later.

00:15:06.600 --> 00:15:07.940
See you.

00:15:09.530 --> 00:15:13.380
Alice wasn't really welcome at first,

00:15:14.250 --> 00:15:17.240
but I couldn't tell that at all.

00:15:17.800 --> 00:15:21.380
C-Could it be that they looked coldly at me, too?!

00:15:22.260 --> 00:15:24.400
What should I do if that's the case...

00:15:24.750 --> 00:15:26.740
That's... That's so scary...

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:29.500
And what happened next?

00:15:30.490 --> 00:15:32.700
Ah, about Alice?

00:15:33.140 --> 00:15:36.470
For a while, they didn't really fight each other.

00:15:37.720 --> 00:15:39.560
Even if she gave out orders enthusiastically,

00:15:39.560 --> 00:15:42.060
everyone just didn't feel like following.

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:51.810
Now that I think of it, Section III was still looking for its identity back then.

00:15:52.480 --> 00:15:54.740
What we can actually do...

00:15:54.740 --> 00:15:56.220
About what we should do...

00:15:57.410 --> 00:16:00.750
And then one event changed everything for us.

00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:04.300
We shall be going to arrest Major Ranke.

00:16:04.300 --> 00:16:05.310
Are you serious?!

00:16:05.830 --> 00:16:07.410
I read the report.

00:16:07.410 --> 00:16:10.300
Taking into consideration the current situation of the Northern frontline area,

00:16:10.300 --> 00:16:13.500
the major's corruption makes him a war aggravator.

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:15.080
Persuading him to stop is out of the question.

00:16:17.270 --> 00:16:18.080
What's the matter?

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:19.950
Do we stand a chance?

00:16:20.470 --> 00:16:21.790
Chance?

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:26.170
Our chances of arresting the major,
prosecuting him, and finding him guilty.

00:16:26.740 --> 00:16:30.510
We haven't been able to do anything because our chances of doing that were low.

00:16:30.510 --> 00:16:31.840
We have no chance!

00:16:33.090 --> 00:16:36.820
If we rely on our chances,
we won't be able to accomplish anything.

00:16:36.820 --> 00:16:37.840
But...

00:16:37.840 --> 00:16:40.390
If we fail, then we could be punished for this.

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:41.340
There's no point-

00:16:41.340 --> 00:16:42.170
Machs.

00:16:42.700 --> 00:16:44.270
Who does Section III exist for?

00:16:45.550 --> 00:16:46.570
For the army?

00:16:46.970 --> 00:16:48.770
For those perpetrating injustice?

00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:51.780
For giving you and me food to eat?

00:16:59.860 --> 00:17:02.130
Section III exists for the people.

00:17:02.130 --> 00:17:04.750
If we back down for self-preservation,

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:09.030
then Section III will bear
the same guilt as the people doing injustice.

00:17:09.030 --> 00:17:10.370
That's...

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:13.770
Where is the evidence of the major's wrongdoing?

00:17:13.770 --> 00:17:15.750
Inside the safe in his office.

00:17:16.170 --> 00:17:17.070
Okay!

00:17:17.070 --> 00:17:18.760
Imperial S.S. III, prepare for sortie!

00:17:19.250 --> 00:17:22.690
We're going to go into a military facility without a warrant?

00:17:22.690 --> 00:17:24.690
Boss, stop her.

00:17:24.690 --> 00:17:27.270
Ah, I got one right here.

00:17:28.840 --> 00:17:30.670
You're doing this, too, Boss?

00:17:30.670 --> 00:17:36.410
But man, I really don't know how to deal with people that can just say things like that.

00:17:37.460 --> 00:17:39.940
What, you're on that side, too?

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:45.590
What do you guys want?!

00:17:46.410 --> 00:17:48.050
Imperial S.S. III!

00:17:48.050 --> 00:17:51.520
We regard Major Ranke's corruption as war aggravation...

00:17:51.520 --> 00:17:53.090
...and will proceed to arrest him.

00:17:55.890 --> 00:17:58.420
Who do you think you're talking to, 2nd Lieutenant?

00:17:58.860 --> 00:18:02.220
Disrespect for a superior is considered treason, you know?

00:18:02.420 --> 00:18:04.140
Rank is irrelevant now.

00:18:04.660 --> 00:18:07.090
And what's that piece of paper going to do?

00:18:07.090 --> 00:18:09.440
Machs, is this your work?

00:18:09.440 --> 00:18:10.770
N-No-

00:18:10.930 --> 00:18:12.410
There's no use in talking!

00:18:12.410 --> 00:18:14.090
We're going to confiscate evidence.

00:18:14.090 --> 00:18:15.320
Open up your safe.

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:18.780
Do you think you'll be fine after doing something like this?

00:18:18.990 --> 00:18:20.810
That is none of my business!

00:18:20.810 --> 00:18:23.990
And how long will you be able to maintain that bravado?

00:18:24.220 --> 00:18:25.240
Open it!

00:18:25.730 --> 00:18:27.460
You can't pull your sword out.

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:30.020
This is still his command.

00:18:30.020 --> 00:18:31.800
Going to use force, eh?

00:18:40.330 --> 00:18:41.430
They're attempting a coup d'etat.

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:44.220
These people are traitors.

00:18:44.750 --> 00:18:47.360
They want to point a sword at me, a superior officer.

00:18:47.360 --> 00:18:49.730
Now, please calm down, everybody.

00:18:49.730 --> 00:18:51.940
Come on, Lieutenant; be more peaceful.

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:54.350
Major, stop this already!

00:18:54.350 --> 00:18:56.600
Do you want to continue your wrongdoings?

00:18:56.600 --> 00:18:58.750
Quiet, you traitor.

00:18:58.750 --> 00:19:01.410
Do you consider yourself a soldier for going against your superior?!

00:19:02.500 --> 00:19:04.260
You're the traitor!

00:19:04.260 --> 00:19:05.500
You betray your subordinates!

00:19:05.500 --> 00:19:06.700
You betray the army!

00:19:06.700 --> 00:19:08.250
You're betraying the people!

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:09.570
If you still consider yourself a soldier,

00:19:09.570 --> 00:19:11.240
then bow to the ropes of justice.

00:19:11.930 --> 00:19:13.640
So, now you reveal your true colors.

00:19:13.640 --> 00:19:15.170
I don't care; shoot them.

00:19:17.080 --> 00:19:18.810
You cowards.

00:19:18.810 --> 00:19:20.360
Rudolf, shoot them.

00:19:20.360 --> 00:19:21.930
Y-Yes, sir.

00:19:27.880 --> 00:19:30.330
I suggest you don't, Mr. Elite.

00:19:30.330 --> 00:19:36.150
This person here is a famous Malvin of the Thirteen Appointed Families's daughter.

00:19:37.240 --> 00:19:37.900
Is that true?

00:19:38.400 --> 00:19:41.020
Shoot her and you'll be entering hell.

00:19:41.020 --> 00:19:43.910
A death sentence might be on the light side.

00:19:44.140 --> 00:19:46.160
What are you two mumbling about?

00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:48.660
Ah, just a little grown-up talk.

00:19:49.090 --> 00:19:50.180
What are you doing?

00:19:50.180 --> 00:19:50.770
Shoot her.

00:19:51.630 --> 00:19:53.470
Don't be scared, Rudolf!

00:19:53.470 --> 00:19:56.170
If you don't, we're doomed!

00:19:59.660 --> 00:20:00.260
Don't!

00:20:01.670 --> 00:20:02.590
Careful!

00:20:07.990 --> 00:20:09.240
Machs!

00:20:10.030 --> 00:20:11.500
He died?!

00:20:14.380 --> 00:20:16.340
What are you talking about?

00:20:16.340 --> 00:20:20.390
That would mean that Machs is a ghost right now.

00:20:20.740 --> 00:20:22.150
You're right.

00:20:23.070 --> 00:20:25.950
Machs' injury wasn't too serious,

00:20:25.950 --> 00:20:28.490
and the evidence of corruption was confiscated.

00:20:28.910 --> 00:20:31.440
That event changed everything.

00:20:31.440 --> 00:20:33.850
Section III finally became Section III.

00:20:34.660 --> 00:20:36.000
Here, all done.

00:20:38.590 --> 00:20:39.840
Sorry for the trouble.

00:20:40.580 --> 00:20:43.430
Do you know the meaning of this emblem, Corporal?

00:20:44.030 --> 00:20:45.590
Alice came up with it.

00:20:47.060 --> 00:20:48.350
The lieutenant did?

00:20:48.910 --> 00:20:52.310
She said an emblem is necessary to rally everyone together.

00:20:52.860 --> 00:20:57.040
The speech she gave when
she revealed this was very moving.

00:20:59.600 --> 00:21:03.740
"The obstacles that we encounter every time in our missions..."

00:21:03.740 --> 00:21:07.310
"...are war aggravators that take things away from civilians for their own greed."

00:21:07.830 --> 00:21:10.740
"They are always in a place where we cannot reach."

00:21:11.340 --> 00:21:12.740
"Using money, violence"...

00:21:12.740 --> 00:21:14.850
...and power, they are inside numerous layers of protection.

00:21:15.290 --> 00:21:19.080
Yes, like the skin of a very thick pumpkin.

00:21:19.720 --> 00:21:21.240
We need a blade.

00:21:21.240 --> 00:21:25.070
Scissors that we use to decorate our pumpkins the night before Halloween...

00:21:25.070 --> 00:21:28.030
We need a powerful blade like those pumpkin scissors...

00:21:29.010 --> 00:21:31.720
...in order to cut apart the outer skin, however hard it is.

00:21:32.450 --> 00:21:34.480
That's why we shall call ourselves...

00:21:34.480 --> 00:21:35.830
...with pride...

00:21:35.830 --> 00:21:37.740
Pumpkin Scissors!

00:21:41.570 --> 00:21:44.750
She told me that I can't rest with light injuries like this.

00:21:44.750 --> 00:21:46.150
She makes us work too hard.

00:21:47.270 --> 00:21:51.530
The people are waiting for the revival
of this country like waiting for Spring to come.

00:21:52.090 --> 00:21:54.040
We are not allowed to stay idle.

00:23:30.980 --> 00:23:34.380
Mer-kun, we're going to get interviewed by the newspaper!

00:23:34.780 --> 00:23:36.800
Oh, now's not the time for this!

00:23:36.800 --> 00:23:38.970
Alice got kidnapped?!

00:23:39.480 --> 00:23:41.770
Next time, "The Quiet Quickening".

00:23:41.770 --> 00:23:43.980
Come get us if you're not scared!
